DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x)^2)^3");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^((e^(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[7, infinity) U {-5, -4, -2, 3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -2, 3}) U [7, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("([7, infinity) - [7, infinity))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("([7, infinity)) U (((-infinity, 19] U [2, infinity)))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[7, infinity) U [7, infinity) U [2, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("([2, infinity)) U [7, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

[`19*18+16*1`] is equal to [_____]{358}
---

What is the value of [`0+10+7`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('17'),width=>6}
---

[`11*14+0*17`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>154,width=>9}
---

What is the value of [`16+1+11-9/11`]? [_____]{Real(27.1818181818)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 19\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C) \cup ((B \cup A)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`C \cup C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -4, -2, 3\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cap B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 1, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -4, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, 2, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 1, 1>") . Compute("<7, -4, 4>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 2, 6>") x Compute("<7, -4, 4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-9, 1, 1>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, -4, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 2, 6>") . Compute("<7, -4, 4>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, -10, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 4, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -2, -5, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, -5, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, 4, 0>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, -5, 5>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, 0>") . Compute("<-10, -10, 1>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>8)}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>0)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
